Root Cause Analysis - Issue 1 (Login)
Version: v 1.0
Date: 2026-08-14
Status: Draft

Incident summary
Floor 6 Legal experienced slow or failed sign-in after recent Win11 and Intune migration activity.

Business impact
- Start-of-day disruption for affected users.
- High urgency due to inability to begin work.

Evidence reviewed
- Same-floor multi-user impact pattern.
- Timing aligned to change window.
- Recovery observed after scoped containment and re-sync actions.

Survived hypothesis
Shared sign-in policy/profile-state drift or misapplied configuration in the migrated baseline.

Cause statement
Most likely root cause is shared configuration drift in the sign-in/profile path for the migrated cohort.

Actions taken
- Scoped incident and validated pattern.
- Reviewed recent sign-in/profile changes.
- Paused/rolled back suspected policy for impacted scope.
- Re-synced devices and re-tested users.

Verification
- Affected user login succeeded.
- No immediate repeat reports in verification window.

Open items
- Exact misconfigured value and change artifact ID to confirm.

Preventive actions
- Staged rollout gates.
- Explicit sign-in health checks before expansion.
- Rollback triggers and post-change monitoring.
